### Importing ApiResponse decorators

Source: https://github.com/nestjs/swagger/blob/master/_autodocs/api-reference/api-responses.md

Required imports for using response decorators in a NestJS application.

```typescript
import { ApiResponse, ApiOkResponse, ApiDefaultResponse } from '@nestjs/swagger';
```

--------------------------------

### Import ApiProperty decorators from @nestjs/swagger

Source: https://github.com/nestjs/swagger/blob/master/_autodocs/api-reference/api-property.md

Import the three public decorators from the package root. This is the standard way to use them in a NestJS DTO class.

```typescript
import { ApiProperty, ApiPropertyOptional, ApiResponseProperty } from '@nestjs/swagger';
```

--------------------------------

### Using ApiResponse with DTOs and status codes

Source: https://github.com/nestjs/swagger/blob/master/_autodocs/api-reference/api-responses.md

Example of applying multiple ApiResponse decorators to a route handler to define different status responses.

```typescript
@Get(':id')
@ApiResponse({ status: 200, type: CatDto, description: 'The cat' })
@ApiResponse({ status: 404, description: 'Cat not found' })
@ApiResponse({ status: '5XX', description: 'Server error' })
getCat(@Param('id') id: string) {
  // ...
}
```

--------------------------------

### SwaggerModule.createDocument Method Signature

Source: https://github.com/nestjs/swagger/blob/master/_autodocs/api-reference/swagger-module.md

The static method signature for creating an OpenAPI document from an initialized NestJS application.

```typescript
public static createDocument(
    app: INestApplication,
    config: Omit<OpenAPIObject, 'paths'>,
    options: SwaggerDocumentOptions = {}
): OpenAPIObject
```

--------------------------------

### Disabling the UI and restricting raw definitions to JSON only

Source: https://github.com/nestjs/swagger/blob/master/_autodocs/api-reference/swagger-module.md

Example of setting up Swagger with the UI disabled and raw definitions restricted to JSON only, using the 'ui' and 'raw' options.

```typescript
SwaggerModule.setup('/api-docs', app, document, {
  ui: false,
  raw: ['json']
});
```
